                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Tyranny is an underrated and forgotten gem from Obsidian. Honestly, I liked this one way more than their Pillars of Eternity series, and I would totally play Tyranny 2 instead of whatever Obsidian has done in recent years.\n\nSadly, nothing is perfect, and this game is no exception. Companion AI here is very basic, meaning you will not be able to customize it in depth. Crafting is, well, weird and questionable. I didn't have to use potions outside of healing ones even on the highest difficulty setting, so crafting them was pointless, especially since crafting basically requires you to \"select what you want and walk on the world map for a couple of minutes\". Gear upgrades, on the other hand, were straightforward and easy.\n\nI mean, the biggest problem with this game is that there is no Tyranny 2. The game ends on a cliffhanger, right where the story goes into second gear. With its funny dialogue, decent characters to explore, intrigues, and replayability, this game had everything and yet, it was abandoned. It makes me sad.\n\nSo, if none of the issues above stop you, then yes, it is totally worth a try.",
